      ],
      "text": "**Today is Saturday, October 17, 2026.** If your children have a Saturday school session, I’d **keep them home if they have asthma or other breathing problems, are coughing/wheezing, or you’re worried about their health**—and let the school know.\n\nThe latest KL reading I found was **API 164 (unhealthy)** at 18:00 MYT. That’s below the current **school-closure threshold of over 200**, but outdoor school activities should stop above 100. Malaysia’s Education Minister has also said parents may keep children home over haze concerns if they notify the school. ([hazemonitor.com](https://hazemonitor.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\nFor children who feel well, whether to attend is your call; I’d first check the school’s latest notice and the **official APIMS reading for the station nearest the school**, since levels can change and differ by area. If they go, ask the school to keep them indoors and skip outdoor PE/sports. ([eqms.doe.gov.my](https://eqms.doe.gov.my/apims/main?utm_source=openai))",
